Title: XP/Vista source fixes outside third_party/winwrap
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

The home for source changes legacy Windows needs that are not winwrap's job.
winwrap substitutes missing Win32 functions wholesale (see
18-winwrap-library.patch); this patch is for the cases better answered where
the call is made.

First of those: Electron calls shell32's SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID
and GetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID unconditionally, from four places
across shell/common, shell/browser and shell/renderer. Both are Windows 7 and
later. Vista has shell32, just an older one without them.

That combination is worse than it sounds. shell32 is delay-imported, so the
missing export is not fatal at load, and the process starts normally; the
failure lands on the first call, inside Chromium's delay-load failure hook,
which ends in NOTREACHED(). In a release build that is an int3, so Windows
reports APPCRASH with exception code 0x80000003, an offset, and nothing else --
no module name, no function name. It took a minidump and a PDB to learn which
of 48 delay-loaded DLLs was involved.

Resolved with GetProcAddress instead, through two wrappers in
application_info_win.cc, returning E_NOTIMPL where the export is absent.
Nothing downstream needed restructuring: E_NOTIMPL is a failure, and failure is
what Windows already returns from Get for a process that never called Set, so
GetRawAppUserModelID() takes its existing branch and derives an ID from the
application name. Set's callers never looked at the result.

Deliberately not left to winwrap, which can also supply these. winwrap only
links when use_winwrap is on, which is the --xp args and not an ordinary
release build -- so a plain build would still have crashed on Vista. Resolving
at the call site covers every configuration and costs a Win7-and-later user one
cached GetProcAddress.

shell32 is looked up with GetModuleHandleW first, since any process reaching
this has it loaded, and LoadLibraryEx pinned to LOAD_LIBRARY_SEARCH_SYSTEM32 as
a fallback so the name cannot be planted. That flag wants Windows 7, or Vista
with KB2533623, which costs nothing: where the flag is missing, so are the two
functions being looked for.

diff --git a/electron/shell/common/application_info.h b/electron/shell/common/application_info.h
--- a/electron/shell/common/application_info.h
+++ b/electron/shell/common/application_info.h
@@ -32,6 +32,16 @@
 bool IsAppRTL();
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+// shell32's Get/SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID, resolved at runtime
+// because shell32 only exports them on Windows 7 and later. Calling the
+// imports directly is fatal on Vista and XP -- they are delay imports, so the
+// failure surfaces on first call, where Chromium's delay-load failure hook
+// ends in NOTREACHED(). Both report failure where the OS lacks them, which is
+// also what Windows returns when no ID has been set, so callers need no
+// separate path. See application_info_win.cc.
+HRESULT GetExplicitAppUserModelID(PWSTR* app_id);
+HRESULT SetExplicitAppUserModelID(PCWSTR app_id);
+
 PCWSTR GetRawAppUserModelID();
 base::win::ScopedHString GetAppUserModelID();
 void SetAppUserModelID(const std::wstring& name);
diff --git a/electron/shell/common/application_info_win.cc b/electron/shell/common/application_info_win.cc
--- a/electron/shell/common/application_info_win.cc
+++ b/electron/shell/common/application_info_win.cc
@@ -48,15 +48,54 @@
   return base::UTF16ToUTF8(info->product_version());
 }
 
+namespace {
+
+// shell32 is already loaded in any process that gets this far, so a module
+// handle is normally enough; LoadLibraryEx is the fallback, pinned to System32
+// so the name cannot be planted. That flag needs Windows 7 (or Vista with
+// KB2533623), which costs nothing here: on the versions where it is missing,
+// so are the functions being looked for.
+HMODULE Shell32() {
+  static const HMODULE module = []() -> HMODULE {
+    if (HMODULE loaded = ::GetModuleHandleW(L"shell32.dll"))
+      return loaded;
+    return ::LoadLibraryExW(L"shell32.dll", nullptr,
+                            LOAD_LIBRARY_SEARCH_SYSTEM32);
+  }();
+  return module;
+}
+
+}  // namespace
+
+HRESULT GetExplicitAppUserModelID(PWSTR* app_id) {
+  using GetFn = decltype(&::GetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID);
+  static const GetFn get_fn = reinterpret_cast<GetFn>(::GetProcAddress(
+      Shell32(), "GetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID"));
+
+  // Clear the out parameter whatever happens: callers below free it
+  // unconditionally, and Windows leaves it untouched when it fails.
+  if (app_id)
+    *app_id = nullptr;
+  return get_fn ? get_fn(app_id) : E_NOTIMPL;
+}
+
+HRESULT SetExplicitAppUserModelID(PCWSTR app_id) {
+  using SetFn = decltype(&::SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID);
+  static const SetFn set_fn = reinterpret_cast<SetFn>(::GetProcAddress(
+      Shell32(), "SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID"));
+
+  return set_fn ? set_fn(app_id) : E_NOTIMPL;
+}
+
 void SetAppUserModelID(const std::wstring& name) {
   GetAppUserModelId() = name;
-  SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID(GetAppUserModelId().c_str());
+  SetExplicitAppUserModelID(GetAppUserModelId().c_str());
 }
 
 PCWSTR GetRawAppUserModelID() {
   if (GetAppUserModelId().empty()) {
     PWSTR current_app_id;
-    if (SUCCEEDED(GetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID(&current_app_id))) {
+    if (SUCCEEDED(GetExplicitAppUserModelID(&current_app_id))) {
       GetAppUserModelId() = current_app_id;
     } else {
       std::string name = GetApplicationName();
diff --git a/electron/shell/browser/electron_browser_client.cc b/electron/shell/browser/electron_browser_client.cc
--- a/electron/shell/browser/electron_browser_client.cc
+++ b/electron/shell/browser/electron_browser_client.cc
@@ -654,7 +654,7 @@
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
     // Append --app-user-model-id.
     PWSTR current_app_id;
-    if (SUCCEEDED(GetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID(&current_app_id))) {
+    if (SUCCEEDED(GetExplicitAppUserModelID(&current_app_id))) {
       command_line->AppendSwitchNative(switches::kAppUserModelId,
                                        current_app_id);
       CoTaskMemFree(current_app_id);
diff --git a/electron/shell/renderer/renderer_client_base.cc b/electron/shell/renderer/renderer_client_base.cc
--- a/electron/shell/renderer/renderer_client_base.cc
+++ b/electron/shell/renderer/renderer_client_base.cc
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "printing/buildflags/buildflags.h"
 #include "shell/browser/api/electron_api_protocol.h"
 #include "shell/common/api/electron_api_native_image.h"
+#include "shell/common/application_info.h"
 #include "shell/common/color_util.h"
 #include "shell/common/gin_helper/dictionary.h"
 #include "shell/common/js2c_bundle_ids.h"
@@ -310,7 +311,7 @@
   std::wstring app_id =
       command_line->GetSwitchValueNative(switches::kAppUserModelId);
   if (!app_id.empty()) {
-    SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID(app_id.c_str());
+    SetExplicitAppUserModelID(app_id.c_str());
   }
 #endif
 }
